<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Munmu of Silla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/626">626</a>–681</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Munmu was king of Silla from 661 to 681, son of King Muyeol. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang China</a> he completed the conquest of Baekje and destroyed Goguryeo in 668, and then fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silla-tang-war">Silla–Tang War</a>, which ended in 676 with Silla controlling the peninsula south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taedong-river">Taedong River</a>. He asked to be buried at sea to guard the kingdom as a dragon, and his tomb is placed at Daewangam rock.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/munmu-of-silla.jpg" alt="Munmu of Silla" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Christophe95 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portraits_of_kings_at_Tongiljeon.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
